[
  {
    "id": "EX01:aim:1",
    "experiment_id": "EX01",
    "experiment_name": "Program Replacement with exec",
    "topic": "Program Replacement with exec",
    "section_type": "Aim",
    "source": "exec.md",
    "page_section": "Aim #1",
    "language": "en",
    "content_hash": "616d2839043fa0f2e7b3a976195bff7bfb69e29902f8b790264b3ac0e55df97a",
    "text": "Replace a child process image with another program."
  },
  {
    "id": "EX01:theory:1",
    "experiment_id": "EX01",
    "experiment_name": "Program Replacement with exec",
    "topic": "Program Replacement with exec",
    "section_type": "Theory",
    "source": "exec.md",
    "page_section": "Theory #1",
    "language": "en",
    "content_hash": "781bd4d5a810844b85fe4cfc298fad7f4b00e8e8a47652f380d5e7ba3a112894",
    "text": "A successful exec call does not return. The process ID stays the same while its program image changes."
  },
  {
    "id": "EX01:procedure:1",
    "experiment_id": "EX01",
    "experiment_name": "Program Replacement with exec",
    "topic": "Program Replacement with exec",
    "section_type": "Procedure",
    "source": "exec.md",
    "page_section": "Procedure #1",
    "language": "en",
    "content_hash": "66518a9f0b0e3a39d21fe3c4fcc6e729614a17efd53f018d55f88fa5e87b650a",
    "text": "Call fork. In the child, call execlp with a valid executable and arguments. Handle the error path only if exec returns. The parent waits."
  },
  {
    "id": "EX01:program:1",
    "experiment_id": "EX01",
    "experiment_name": "Program Replacement with exec",
    "topic": "Program Replacement with exec",
    "section_type": "Program",
    "source": "exec.md",
    "page_section": "Program #1",
    "language": "C",
    "content_hash": "694c723a6b85d3bab333d653448816e7654f2512a8fee0815b073a06aec2610b",
    "text": "The child calls execlp(\"echo\", \"echo\", \"hello\", (char *)NULL); perror follows only on failure."
  },
  {
    "id": "EX01:expected_output:1",
    "experiment_id": "EX01",
    "experiment_name": "Program Replacement with exec",
    "topic": "Program Replacement with exec",
    "section_type": "Expected Output",
    "source": "exec.md",
    "page_section": "Expected Output #1",
    "language": "en",
    "content_hash": "5b97ddfa86005c1ecb6671b8e935e218f786bd65e576afebb2c95e7828cfbffd",
    "text": "The replacement program prints hello. A successful exec does not execute statements following the call."
  },
  {
    "id": "EX01:troubleshooting:1",
    "experiment_id": "EX01",
    "experiment_name": "Program Replacement with exec",
    "topic": "Program Replacement with exec",
    "section_type": "Troubleshooting",
    "source": "exec.md",
    "page_section": "Troubleshooting #1",
    "language": "en",
    "content_hash": "84cdd91e8619bf3254d095e02037a3aef826a5e89ad7f2a4cb8bc19c46802fda",
    "text": "If code after exec runs, check the executable path and arguments; exec may have failed. Always inspect perror and the return path."
  },
  {
    "id": "EX01:viva:1",
    "experiment_id": "EX01",
    "experiment_name": "Program Replacement with exec",
    "topic": "Program Replacement with exec",
    "section_type": "Viva",
    "source": "exec.md",
    "page_section": "Viva #1",
    "language": "en",
    "content_hash": "1f2874ad4fe8b01c0554d429676598a7bf45cffed227a31a7a532ad0552b95db",
    "text": "Does exec create a new process? What happens to the process ID after exec?"
  },
  {
    "id": "FW01:aim:1",
    "experiment_id": "FW01",
    "experiment_name": "Process Creation with fork and wait",
    "topic": "Process Creation with fork and wait",
    "section_type": "Aim",
    "source": "fork_wait.md",
    "page_section": "Aim #1",
    "language": "en",
    "content_hash": "725d3c1de278b77899688f78306e1dd613998550e18481f5d868719c53f524f9",
    "text": "Create a child process and synchronize the parent with its completion."
  },
  {
    "id": "FW01:theory:1",
    "experiment_id": "FW01",
    "experiment_name": "Process Creation with fork and wait",
    "topic": "Process Creation with fork and wait",
    "section_type": "Theory",
    "source": "fork_wait.md",
    "page_section": "Theory #1",
    "language": "en",
    "content_hash": "0abed3f524954fed3d8421e2ecbd8951a96b879fac8a6a4cd15e2c4c8b16995f",
    "text": "fork creates a child process. The return value is zero in the child and positive in the parent. Process scheduling is nondeterministic. wait or waitpid blocks the parent until a child terminates and reaps it."
  },
  {
    "id": "FW01:procedure:1",
    "experiment_id": "FW01",
    "experiment_name": "Process Creation with fork and wait",
    "topic": "Process Creation with fork and wait",
    "section_type": "Procedure",
    "source": "fork_wait.md",
    "page_section": "Procedure #1",
    "language": "en",
    "content_hash": "9d281ba4a1c9a0d97fb8c72dfc659b3fbf4db957d3bb07398b589f8b4cde65b0",
    "text": "Call fork, check failure, run child work in the child branch, call waitpid in the parent branch, and print completion after the wait returns."
  },
  {
    "id": "FW01:program:1",
    "experiment_id": "FW01",
    "experiment_name": "Process Creation with fork and wait",
    "topic": "Process Creation with fork and wait",
    "section_type": "Program",
    "source": "fork_wait.md",
    "page_section": "Program #1",
    "language": "C",
    "content_hash": "fba46c8a9990584227912bc07c869ce754d9ea98cd82f45ea7faec28ba75e95e",
    "text": "The parent branch calls waitpid(child_pid, &status, 0). The child branch exits after its work. Check fork return values and waitpid errors."
  },
  {
    "id": "FW01:expected_output:1",
    "experiment_id": "FW01",
    "experiment_name": "Process Creation with fork and wait",
    "topic": "Process Creation with fork and wait",
    "section_type": "Expected Output",
    "source": "fork_wait.md",
    "page_section": "Expected Output #1",
    "language": "en",
    "content_hash": "9a300562c9ec33bd4986e8123a0b1d3d8e1ba2d81f81eaa63af50dd15c18e2e6",
    "text": "Child work finishes before the parent prints its completion message. Exact process IDs and scheduling order of earlier messages may vary."
  },
  {
    "id": "FW01:troubleshooting:1",
    "experiment_id": "FW01",
    "experiment_name": "Process Creation with fork and wait",
    "topic": "Process Creation with fork and wait",
    "section_type": "Troubleshooting",
    "source": "fork_wait.md",
    "page_section": "Troubleshooting #1",
    "language": "en",
    "content_hash": "bf12f78c80f16a7d8616f97938b757be9d4aa110307d0534a0f40cc477c663fa",
    "text": "If the parent prints completion before the child finishes, inspect the parent branch for a missing wait or waitpid call. A wait in the child branch does not synchronize the parent."
  },
  {
    "id": "FW01:viva:1",
    "experiment_id": "FW01",
    "experiment_name": "Process Creation with fork and wait",
    "topic": "Process Creation with fork and wait",
    "section_type": "Viva",
    "source": "fork_wait.md",
    "page_section": "Viva #1",
    "language": "en",
    "content_hash": "314783420ca005e1b1b47345149d929b46ef1b052de7ced691815ebc776ec613",
    "text": "Why is output order without wait nondeterministic? What does waitpid return? What is a zombie process?"
  },
  {
    "id": "PI01:aim:1",
    "experiment_id": "PI01",
    "experiment_name": "Parent-child communication with pipe",
    "topic": "Parent-child communication with pipe",
    "section_type": "Aim",
    "source": "pipe.md",
    "page_section": "Aim #1",
    "language": "en",
    "content_hash": "f40b665c98be57190be91605c1c013cd2258a20d58daddfb70da2ed82611d046",
    "text": "Send a message from parent to child through a pipe."
  },
  {
    "id": "PI01:theory:1",
    "experiment_id": "PI01",
    "experiment_name": "Parent-child communication with pipe",
    "topic": "Parent-child communication with pipe",
    "section_type": "Theory",
    "source": "pipe.md",
    "page_section": "Theory #1",
    "language": "en",
    "content_hash": "05b5e6fa1b8a5753830d3906ccf2a13ddee78edb194bf3207fa96a60698a8f58",
    "text": "pipe creates a read end and a write end. Unused ends should be closed in each process. A reader sees EOF only after all write ends close."
  },
  {
    "id": "PI01:procedure:1",
    "experiment_id": "PI01",
    "experiment_name": "Parent-child communication with pipe",
    "topic": "Parent-child communication with pipe",
    "section_type": "Procedure",
    "source": "pipe.md",
    "page_section": "Procedure #1",
    "language": "en",
    "content_hash": "0ba027e5eab2113e22eef6c38d0e31261551a33851f0437a2a31da5987d5abc6",
    "text": "Create the pipe before fork. The child closes the write end and reads. The parent closes the read end, writes a message, closes the write end, and waits."
  },
  {
    "id": "PI01:program:1",
    "experiment_id": "PI01",
    "experiment_name": "Parent-child communication with pipe",
    "topic": "Parent-child communication with pipe",
    "section_type": "Program",
    "source": "pipe.md",
    "page_section": "Program #1",
    "language": "C",
    "content_hash": "9ba5a81aa7bbe4c975c3760d44b95b1439f80dc0d96db8f9057bf8b2697cc8af",
    "text": "Use pipe(fd), fork(), close(fd[1]) in the child, close(fd[0]) in the parent, read and write the corresponding ends."
  },
  {
    "id": "PI01:expected_output:1",
    "experiment_id": "PI01",
    "experiment_name": "Parent-child communication with pipe",
    "topic": "Parent-child communication with pipe",
    "section_type": "Expected Output",
    "source": "pipe.md",
    "page_section": "Expected Output #1",
    "language": "en",
    "content_hash": "7b12956806fea3c894990cf7d4818fab832d75fdb6359a95f0e403fa3ec17524",
    "text": "The child receives the bytes written by the parent and exits; the parent reaps the child."
  },
  {
    "id": "PI01:troubleshooting:1",
    "experiment_id": "PI01",
    "experiment_name": "Parent-child communication with pipe",
    "topic": "Parent-child communication with pipe",
    "section_type": "Troubleshooting",
    "source": "pipe.md",
    "page_section": "Troubleshooting #1",
    "language": "en",
    "content_hash": "30d8850b7fff306f08952b98089d6c81fef6df078922369359346ef321f5544d",
    "text": "If a read waits forever, verify every process closes its unused write end. If read fails, verify the child uses fd[0]."
  },
  {
    "id": "PI01:viva:1",
    "experiment_id": "PI01",
    "experiment_name": "Parent-child communication with pipe",
    "topic": "Parent-child communication with pipe",
    "section_type": "Viva",
    "source": "pipe.md",
    "page_section": "Viva #1",
    "language": "en",
    "content_hash": "942f44bbada5e86a1371478328b5f333edda1021fd1802833b52988c73f13f98",
    "text": "What does read return at EOF? Why close unused pipe ends?"
  }
]
